From: CatPlay port <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800: silence the unfilterable "mgmt err" printk

rwnx_rx_mgmt() drops management frames whose length is implausible and
announces each one with a bare printk(). Having no KERN_ prefix, that
logs at the default level, so it cannot be filtered from the console with
`dmesg -n` and it is not routed through the driver's AICWFDBG macros
either. With the CatPlay AP up it fires ~6 times per second.

The console here is the Rockchip FIQ-backed ttyFIQ0, which is also the
only way to reach the board (the image has no other login path and no
DHCP client on the station interface). Flooding it at that rate makes the
board unusable over UART, which removes the one diagnostic channel
available for the USB gadget work this port depends on.

Measured on the ROCK 2A: the line appears only while the AP is running,
so it correlates exactly with hostapd being up. The ttyFIQ console had
overflow counters incremented and the board stopped echoing commands.

The frame is still dropped; only the log is gone. The verdict this
printk reports is itself suspicious -- several frames a second of length
<= 24 or > 768 should not be normal -- but changing the drop policy at
the same time as the logging would make both impossible to attribute, so
this patch deliberately keeps the behaviour identical.

Silenced by CatPlay rather than removed: the check is worth keeping, and
a future investigation of the frame lengths can reintroduce a ratelimited
diagnostic.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor out-of-tree driver, board-local workaround]

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/aic/aic8800_usb/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_rx.c b/drivers/net/wireless/aic/aic8800_usb/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_rx.c
index 0f897c968c4f..16a2ced9d91b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/aic/aic8800_usb/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/aic/aic8800_usb/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_rx.c
@@ -724,7 +724,13 @@ static void rwnx_rx_mgmt(struct rwnx_hw *rwnx_hw, struct rwnx_vif *rwnx_vif,
 
     if (ieee80211_is_mgmt(mgmt->frame_control) &&
         (skb->len <= 24 || skb->len > 768)) {
-        printk("mgmt err\n");
+        /*
+         * Silenced by CatPlay. This is a bare printk() with no KERN_ level,
+         * so it logs at the default level and cannot be filtered with
+         * dmesg -n; with the AP up it fires several times a second and
+         * floods the ttyFIQ serial console until the board is unusable
+         * over UART. The frame is still dropped -- only the log went away.
+         */
         return;
     }
     if (ieee80211_is_beacon(mgmt->frame_control)) {
